WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:18,540
Can you tell me your thoughts on LDN, low dose neltruxone, would it be combined with mistletoe?

00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:26,300
So low dose neltruxone is an off label use of the drug neltruxone.

00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:33,040
Neltruxone is ruled that I think it was 50 milligrams or people getting off of heavy

00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:40,440
drug drugs like morphine. Neltruxone is used to help get people off of drugs like morphine,

00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:48,320
street drugs, people that are addicted to drugs. But that's at 50 milligrams.

00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:52,820
Someone I don't know who it was, I don't remember the story, that found that using it

00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:58,020
in a low, low dose, starting at 1.5 milligrams, point up to 3 milligrams, and then up to

00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:05,020
the maximum 4.5 milligrams, it's called low dose neltruxone. So they're using it off label.

00:01:05,020 --> 00:01:11,680
When you use a drug off label, you're using it for something that it wasn't technically approved

00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:18,180
of by the FDA. So if it wasn't approved by the FDA for that, you're using it off label

00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:24,960
needed for some other thing. Low dose neltruxone has been used for auto-immune diseases because

00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:34,080
it tends to be an immune balancer or an immune regulator or what's called a T cell regulator.

00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:41,080
It acts as stimulating what are called T-reg cells. So when a person is auto-immune and their

00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:49,760
immune system is flared against something, with auto-immune, it's flared against self-tissue,

00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:58,880
and then low dose neltruxone can call that down. Now, there's been some alternative doctors

00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:10,880
that have used low dose neltruxone for cancer, which I don't know. To me, I struggle with

00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:17,920
understanding pathways with that because it really acts like a T-regulator and you really

00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:23,840
want to stimulate the immune system. That's the whole idea of mistletoe therapy. Mistletoe therapy

00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:32,320
is an immune irritant. That's how it works. As an immune irritant, it's firing a hyper-immune response,

00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:41,120
and then with that hyper-T cell stimulation, you're going to possibly kill more cancer cells.

00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:48,400
So I don't know why you would use low dose neltruxone combined with mistletoe.

00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:57,200
To me, it's kind of culture-productive. So I would ask the doctor, if they're prescribing this,

00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:04,640
why they would prescribe it that way. I'm not quite sure that seems culture-productive.

00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:11,820
Do you think there would be positive results with my breast cancer? With mistletoe, for sure,

00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:19,340
that's possible. But low dose neltruxone, no, we have used, we've had people on low dose neltruxone

00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:24,940
with autoimmune disease. I haven't really recommended it. Of course, I don't recommend it,

00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:30,220
because it is a drug, but I haven't. I wouldn't really necessarily think it would be a good fit

00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:35,820
for cancer, even though I know that they're some alternative cancer doctors that do use it. Of course,

00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:41,580
that's not the only thing that they're using. So I'd question whether that is really the thing

00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:49,180
that's helping the person I don't know.

